<body>
  <article>
    <header>
      <h1>Tini's Mac and Cheese</h1>
      <p class="source">
        Recipe transcribed from <a href="https://www.tiktok.com/@tinekeyounger/video/7432820403464146219" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">@tinekeyounger on TikTok</a>
      </p>
    </header>

    <section>
      <h2>Ingredients</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>1 lb cavatappi pasta</li>
        <li>3 tbsp butter</li>
        <li>3 tbsp flour</li>
        <li>1 can (12 oz) evaporated milk</li>
        <li>2 cups heavy cream</li>
        <li>1 tbsp Dijon mustard (optional)</li>
        <li>Shredded cheese blend (split into two bowls)</li>
        <li>Chives, for garnish (optional)</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Seasoning Blend</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Salt (start with ~1 tsp, adjust to taste)</li>
        <li>Pepper (start with ~1 tsp, adjust to taste)</li>
        <li>Smoked paprika (start with ~1 tsp, adjust to taste)</li>
        <li>1 tbsp garlic powder</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Instructions</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>Preheat your oven to 350°F.</li>
        <li>Bring a pot of water to a boil and salt it heavily ("like the ocean"). Boil the cavatappi pasta for 8 minutes if baking immediately, or 7 minutes if preparing ahead of time.</li>
        <li>Shred all of the cheese, mix it together, and split it into two bowls.</li>
        <li>Mix the salt, pepper, smoked paprika, and garlic powder together in a small container.</li>
        <li>Melt 3 tablespoons of butter in a pan over medium heat. Add half of the seasoning blend and let it bloom for 30 seconds.</li>
        <li>Add the flour and cook for 2–3 minutes.</li>
        <li>Gradually pour in the evaporated milk and let it cook for about a minute. Stir in the Dijon mustard (if using).</li>
        <li>Gradually pour in the heavy cream, mixing as you go, and let it cook for about 2 minutes.</li>
        <li>Gradually add half of the shredded cheese, making sure each batch is completely melted before adding more. Stir in the remaining half of the seasoning blend.</li>
        <li>Once all the cheese is melted, fold the cooked pasta into the cheese sauce.</li>
        <li>In a baking dish, add half of the mac and cheese, top with a layer of shredded cheese, add the remaining mac and cheese, and finish with the rest of the shredded cheese on top.</li>
        <li>Bake at 350°F for 25–30 minutes until the cheese on top is melted.</li>
        <li><em>Optional:</em> Switch the oven to broil for 2 minutes to brown the top, then garnish with chives before serving.</li>
      </ol>
    </section>
